<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="a153e6b0">&lt;p&gt;
    Business interviewing is a method for conducting qualitative research to understand specific topics through
    conversation and questions.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Interviewing differs from other methods of data collection in that it is more exploratory in nature and allows for more
    flexibility. Interviewing stems from the desire to know more about the client organization and to better understand how
    key issues affect the client.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
    Business interviewing is most effective when the goal of client research is to gain insight into the &quot;subjective
    understanding&quot; of the organization. By asking clients questions, the project team is enabled to not only observe the
    client&apos;s goals but also understand the reasons behind client performance and issues and to have these reasons explained
    through the client&apos;s responses.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
